<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal to consider plan to ease housing shortage.</title>
<headline>Portugal to consider plan to ease housing shortage.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's Employment Minister Maria Joao Rodrigues will meet construction industry officials next Monday to discuss a plan to ease Portugal's housing shortage, the Association of Construction and Public Works Companies (AECOPS) said.</p>
<p>The plan by AECOPS involves the state financing residential housing construction and should reduce the number of unemployed as more workers are hired to build residential buildings, a statement said.</p>
<p>The additional employment would permit the government to redirect state unemployment subsidies to housing construction and would ultimately lead to lower rents, it added.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
